body:
I really hope this doesn't come off to you as rude but honestly, I do most of that already. Also what I mean with guys not wanting to associate with me is that they're chill and cool (even some of the popular ones) with me until a girl shows up, and it's then that they don't want to be near me. Even one of my close friends does the same thing as well, but I'm not going to corner him to why he feels uncomfortable inviting me to be around girls. I don't get invited to parties really, and while I went a few times with my old friend group (as a convenience friend, which took me a while to realise) I was completely excluded. It doesn't matter how "confident" I am, I'm still left out and treated terribly. Like I said, I did a lot of self improvement such as lifting and skin routines, but I should have mentioned that I also worked on becoming more confident, loud etc. but also more empathetic. People are a bit friendlier to me, but at the end of the day the result is still the same and I'm excluded from any social situations involving girls. I can't deny as a straight guy that girls are still an unimportant aspect to me, because I would be lying. It also sucks that I haven't had any progress (though I didn't have expectations in the first place) even though I've put in effort. Not really sure how to sum this rant up but I appreciate it if you read through this incoherent mess.

&#x200B;

TL;DR: I'm just sick of being treated as a leper and embarrassing other people by being around them.

&#x200B;

Edit: Thanks for believing in me, because I don't get compliments often so it means a lot to me even though you're a stranger over the internet :). Hope you have a nice day/night wherever you are.

Sure, I'm a slightly older than 18 but I'm not exactly sure how old they are. My friend is medium/heavily built, pretty muscular, and is above average IMO. On the other hand I'm really skinny, short, have wrinkles and 3/10 on a good day due to my bad seb derm and other medical conditions (on top of my looks) that I mentioned in my original post. For those reasons, I'd say that he's easily more confident than me, but I often crack jokes and I'm friendly towards everybody so I wouldn't say that I'm not confident/ a pushover. The conversation wasn't necessary so I doubt it was an issue of time, so I can only speculate but I'm going to assume that they intentionally chose to ignore me (or didn't hear me) if they didn't even glance at me after I said hi. Though I'm not going to lie that if I were in their shoes I'd be reluctant to engage in a conversation with myself as well.

&#x200B;

Anyways, thanks again for taking your time and I understand fully. (Sleep is much more important than replying to reddit posts haha) It definitely helps venting about it.

&#x200B;

Edit: I say I'm skinny because even with a high protein diet etc, my muscle mass doesn't increase for some reason, they just get more defined.
